# The release signing key of vettid-agent (AGENT-PLAN §2 AG4;
# docs/RELEASING.md). The same key is published on vettid.org.
#
# It checks two things:
#   - the owner's signature over each release's SHA256SUMS
#     (SHA256SUMS.sig, `ssh-keygen -Y sign -n vettid-agent-release`),
#     with scripts/verify-release and the release workflow;
#   - the owner's signature on release tags (git's gpg.format=ssh;
#     `git -c gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile=release/allowed_signers
#     verify-tag v0.2.0`), with scripts/sign-release.
#
# One line per key, in ssh-keygen's allowed signers format (ssh-keygen(1),
# "ALLOWED SIGNERS"): a principal, the namespaces the key may sign for,
# and the public key (the first two fields of the .pub file). For a
# security key made with `ssh-keygen -t ed25519-sk`:
#
#   vettid-release namespaces="git,vettid-agent-release" sk-ssh-ed25519@openssh.com AAAA...
#
# or for a file key made with `ssh-keygen -t ed25519`:
#
#   vettid-release namespaces="git,vettid-agent-release" ssh-ed25519 AAAA...
#
# Only the owner adds or changes the line, from their own public key.
# Until this file holds a key line, scripts/sign-release and
# scripts/verify-release refuse to run.
